    "c30": {
      "anchor": "later#markdown-1",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "label": "17. Later",
      "excerpt": "A sheet's own \"who may update\" setting: Companies will want it, and it fits the",
      "text": "encrypt its data with a single key held by Spell.\nSpell can still read it, but the host can't.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-02T03:49:06.607Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "encrypt its data before saving.\nNeither the host nor Spell could read it, only the people holding its key",
      "offset": 226,
      "edited": "2026-11-02T03:49:48.544Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-02T03:51:19.716Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  \"Marking a document sensitive would make Spell encrypt its data with a single key held by Spell.  Spell can still read it, but the host can't.\"  I wrote \"Spell\" where it said \"the browser\", since Spell holds the key and does all the writes.</p>\n<p>This also makes it much smaller:  there are no keys to hand out, so it's no longer an epic of its own.  The rows below changed to match, and so did RS's crisis note, as Spell's servers can still read those notes.</p>\n<p><b>One thing to check:</b>  someone has to decrypt for readers.  I wrote that the read proxy decrypts whatever the host lets each person read, so the host still decides who, and Spell doesn't gate a read.  But other AT Protocol apps then see only scrambled data, and the proxy sees the contents, though until now it passed everything through unread.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-02T03:51:06.068Z"
      }
    },
    "c31": {
      "anchor": "later#markdown-1",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "label": "17. Later",
      "excerpt": "A sheet's own \"who may update\" setting: Companies will want it, and it fits the",
      "text": "Spell has to decrypt the document before it can be searched.  Losing the key loses the document.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-02T03:50:01.416Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Spell can't search it, project it or check what's inside, and losing the key loses the document.",
      "offset": 414,
      "edited": "2026-11-02T03:50:28.586Z",
      "replies": [
